[2026-09-29 18:55] app-warning: "GET /models failed, using fallback Network Error"
  root cause: adb reverse tunnels (tcp:8000 -> host backend, tcp:8081 -> metro) had silently
  dropped (adb reverse --list was empty); device-side fetch to 127.0.0.1:8000 was refused.
  impact: non-fatal — app used FALLBACK_MODELS (identical list); wakeUp/predict would also
  fail while the tunnel was down.
  fix applied: (1) tunnels re-established (adb reverse --list: host-19 tcp:8081, tcp:8000);
  (2) mobile/src/hooks/useApi.js useModels.refresh now retries 3x with backoff before warning.
  prevention: emulator_ui_driver.ps1 re-asserts both reverses at start of every run.

[2026-09-29 18:36] ui-driver: full run aborted mid-flight (user abort at cycle 17).
  known defects fixed before redo: (a) Wait-Result used To-Bottom -> for known-class results
  the Confidence row sat above the fold (long disease-info page) => false timeouts on cycles
  1-4,6-11,13-17; fix = top-down paged scan. (b) no Save-to-History tap (now added).
  (c) initial keyevent 4 (BACK) at driver start exited the app to launcher (removed earlier).
  (d) picker thumbnail tap race (settled earlier with settle+retry logic).

